Local review patch: propagate T6032 cpufreq initialization failure
Base: reviewed m1n1 2460b604c6f016956ead711823605eea840c602e, after adapted 0001..0010
Provenance: AI-assisted Debian project work; not submitted upstream.

Keep legacy cpufreq best-effort behavior for non-T6032 SoCs. For T6032 only,
stop the kernel payload path before secondary startup when cpufreq
initialization fails. The existing SMP, HV, and proxy caller contracts are
unchanged; the cutoff is local to the native payload boot path.

--- a/src/payload.c
+++ b/src/payload.c
@@ -316,5 +316,7 @@
     if (kernel && fdt) {
-        cpufreq_init();
+        int cpufreq_status = cpufreq_init();
+        if (chip_id == T6032 && cpufreq_status < 0)
+            return -1;
         if (smp_start_secondaries() < 0)
             return -1;
         mitigations_perform();
